2. Mathematical Framework

2.1 Context Space

Let K be a finite connected simplicial complex. We use K_3 (triangle) for minimal computations and the annulus mesh for the decisive falsifier.

2.2 Cellular Sheaf with Restricted Monodromy

Let \mathcal{F} be a cellular sheaf on K with stalks \mathcal{F}(v)\cong\mathbb{R}^d and orthogonal restriction maps \rho_{v\triangleleft e}. The monodromy around a cycle \gamma is M_\gamma=\prod_{e\in\gamma}\rho_{v_e^+\triangleleft e}\rho_{v_e^-\triangleleft e}^{-1}.

Critical correction. A twisted sheaf with M_\gamma\neq I_d does not imply H^1\neq 0. For a cycle graph, \dim H^1=\dim H^0=\dim\ker(M_\gamma-I_d). If M_\gamma is a rotation in \mathbb{R}^2 with no fixed vectors, then H^0=H^1=0: the sheaf is acyclic and every 1-cochain is exact. The frustration appears as a strictly positive spectral gap \lambda_2(L_0)>0, not as cohomology.

Restriction. We require monodromies M_\gamma with non-trivial fixed subspaces: \dim\ker(M_\gamma-I_d)>0. Then H^1(K;\mathcal{F})\neq 0 and cohomology does genuine work. This separates cohomological frustration (fixed-subspace twists) from spectral frustration (fixed-point-free twists).

2.3 Cohomology and Sheaf Laplacian

The cochain complex is 0\to C^0\xrightarrow{\delta_0}C^1\xrightarrow{\delta_1}C^2\to\cdots, with (\delta_0 s)_e=\rho_{v^+\triangleleft e}s_{v^+}-\rho_{v^-\triangleleft e}s_{v^-}. The sheaf Laplacian is L_0=\delta_0^\top\delta_0, with \ker L_0\cong H^0(K;\mathcal{F}) and \lambda_2(L_0) the smallest positive eigenvalue.

2.4 Hodge Decomposition

C^1(K;\mathcal{F})=\operatorname{im}\delta_0\oplus\ker L_1\oplus\operatorname{im}\delta_1^\top,

with \ker L_1\cong H^1(K;\mathcal{F}). Every c\in C^1 decomposes uniquely as c=\delta_0 s+h+\delta_1^\top t.

2.5 Obstructions

\boxed{\Gamma(c)=\|P_{\mathcal{H}^1}c\|_2,\qquad T(s)=\|\delta_0 s\|_2.}

\Gamma(c) is metric-dependent; the cohomology class [c]\in H^1 is topological. We fix the standard inner product throughout.

2.6 Floor Theorem (Restricted to Graphs)

Theorem Q1. For a graph K (no 2-cells, so \operatorname{im}\delta_1^\top=0),

\inf_{s\in C^0}\|c-\delta_0 s\|_2=\Gamma(c).

For a general simplicial complex with 2-cells, the correct statement is

\inf_{s\in C^0}\|c-\delta_0 s\|_2=\|h+\delta_1^\top t\|_2,

since the curl component \delta_1^\top t is also an obstruction that local node adjustments cannot fix.

2.7 Recursive Dynamics

The state is X_t=(s_t,h_t)\in C^0\oplus\mathcal{H}^1 with coupled dynamics

s_{t+1}=s_t-\eta\nabla_s\mathcal{E}(s_t)+A_h h_t,\qquad h_{t+1}=(1-\kappa)h_t+\xi_t.

