8. Three Kill Tests

Q1. Floor theorem (graphs) and cohomological vs spectral obstruction comparison (annulus). Informational necessity.

Q2. Annulus falsifier: triangle penalties blind, \Gamma(c) detects. Dynamical relevance via coupled dynamics.

Q3. Friction-tensor metric, Landauer bound in correct units, speed-cost tradeoff. Thermodynamic interpretability.

If Q1 fails, cohomological component killed. If Q1 succeeds, Q2 fails: cohomology survives as representation, not stability theory. If Q1, Q2 succeed, Q3 fails: mathematical theory without thermodynamics.

