Appendix D. Counter-Examples

D.1 Gauge Drift on K_3

Take K=K_3 with constant sheaf \underline{\mathbb{R}}. Define dynamics s_{t+1}=s_t+\eta\mathbf{1}, \eta>0. Then c_{t+1}=\delta_0 s_{t+1}=\delta_0 s_t=c_t, so \Gamma(c_t)=0 and T(s_t)=T(s_0) for all t. Yet

\|s_t\|_0^2=\|s_0\|_0^2+2t\eta\langle s_0,\mathbf{1}\rangle+t^2\eta^2\|\mathbf{1}\|_0^2
=\|s_0\|_0^2+2t\eta\langle s_0,\mathbf{1}\rangle+3t^2\eta^2\to\infty.

The divergence is quadratic in t. The coefficient 3t^2\eta^2 is the squared norm of the drift vector.

D.2 Generalization to C_n

For the n-cycle with constant sheaf, \ker L_0=\operatorname{span}(\mathbf{1}), \|\mathbf{1}\|_0^2=n, so

\|s_t\|_0^2=\|s_0\|_0^2+2t\eta\langle s_0,\mathbf{1}\rangle+nt^2\eta^2.

The divergence rate scales as \sqrt{n}\,\eta\,t.

D.3 Twisted Sheaf on C_n with Fixed-Point-Free Monodromy

Let \mathcal{F} have stalks \mathbb{R}^2 and monodromy M=R_\theta\in SO(2) with \theta\notin 2\pi\mathbb{Z}. Then \ker(M-I_2)=\{0\}, so H^0=H^1=0. The sheaf is acyclic; every 1-cochain is exact. The frustration is spectral: \lambda_2(L_0)>0. For a cycle of length n,

\lambda_2(L_0)=2-2\cos(\theta/n)\text{ (for the twisted cycle)},

or more generally the smallest positive eigenvalue of the twisted Laplacian. The point: cohomology is zero, but the system is frustrated. This is the complementary case to D.1 and D.2.

D.4 The Annulus as a Non-Vacuous Falsifier

See Appendix G for the full construction. Summary: the annulus has H^1\neq 0, so \Gamma(c) can be non-zero. It has 2-cells, so the triangle penalty \sum_\sigma\|\delta_1 c\|_1^2 is non-trivial. The falsifier constructs c with zero triangle penalty and non-zero \Gamma(c), demonstrating that local penalties are blind to the global obstruction.

