Appendix G. Annulus Falsifier: Explicit Construction

G.1 Triangulation

Let \mathcal{A}_n be an annulus triangulated with n sectors. Vertices: a_1,\ldots,a_n on the inner circle, b_1,\ldots,b_n on the outer circle. Edges:

· Inner: e_i^I=(a_i,a_{i+1}) for i=1,\ldots,n (indices mod n);
· Outer: e_i^O=(b_i,b_{i+1});
· Radial: e_i^R=(a_i,b_i) and e_i^{R'}=(a_{i+1},b_i).

Faces: F_i^1=(a_i,a_{i+1},b_i) and F_i^2=(a_{i+1},b_i,b_{i+1}) for i=1,\ldots,n.

Counts: V=2n, E=4n, F=2n. Euler: V-E+F=0, consistent with the annulus. \dim H^0=1, \dim H^1=1, \dim H^2=0.

G.2 Constant Sheaf Cochains

With \underline{\mathbb{R}}: \dim C^0=2n, \dim C^1=4n, \dim C^2=2n.

Ranks: \mathrm{rank}\,\delta_0=2n-1 (kernel dimension 1). \mathrm{rank}\,\delta_1=2n (by Euler). \mathrm{rank}\,\delta_1^\top=2n.

Hodge: \dim C^1=(2n-1)+1+2n=4n. ✓

G.3 Harmonic 1-Cochain

Let h\in C^1 be the harmonic representative of the generator of H^1(\mathcal{A}_n)\cong\mathbb{R}. It satisfies \delta_0^\top h=0 (divergence-free) and \delta_1 h=0 (curl-free on each triangle).

A concrete construction: set h(e_i^I)=1, h(e_i^O)=1, h(e_i^R)=h(e_i^{R'})=0. This cochain has zero circulation around each triangle (because the radial edges have value 0 and the inner/outer edges are antiparallel in each triangle), so \delta_1 h=0. It is divergence-free at all vertices (check: at each inner vertex, one incoming inner edge +1 and one outgoing inner edge -1 cancel). Hence h\in\ker L_1, and \|h\|_1^2=2n.

G.4 A Locally Exact but Globally Non-Exact Cochain

Take c=\delta_0 s_0+h with s_0 chosen so that \delta_0 s_0 is arbitrary and h as above. Then:

· \delta_1 c=\delta_1\delta_0 s_0+\delta_1 h=0+0=0: triangle penalty vanishes.
· \Gamma(c)=\|P_{\mathcal{H}^1}c\|_1=\|h\|_1=\sqrt{2n}>0.

Thus the triangle-level penalty \sum_\sigma\|\delta_1 c\|_1^2 is zero, while the harmonic measure \Gamma(c) is non-zero. Local penalties are blind; only the harmonic measure sees the obstruction.

G.5 Pre-Registered Falsification Protocol

Hypothesis. There exist cochains c on \mathcal{A}_n with \sum_\sigma\|\delta_1 c\|_1^2=0 and \Gamma(c)>0.

Null. For all c, \sum_\sigma\|\delta_1 c\|_1^2=0\implies\Gamma(c)=0.

Test. Compute both quantities on the explicit c above. If the hypothesis holds, Q2 is answered affirmatively. If the null holds, the cohomological obstruction is dynamically redundant.

Implementation. Numerical verification in sympy/NumPy (see Appendix I).

